{"id":"e0293bf5-4336-488b-828d-c09b39aa36d3","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The parameter 'args' is an array reference provided for the main method and is never null when run from the command line.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.803124Z"}
{"id":"b2e6e65d-6713-48f0-952c-eaca54a55133","expr":"b == 0 || b * (a / b) <= a && b * (a / b) >= (a - Math.abs(b) + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, b * (a / b) provides the largest multiple of b less than or equal to a (for positive b), capturing properties of integer division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805216Z"}
{"id":"75b2e621-e16a-4056-b239-911d1deb9565","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"An array's length is always non-negative in Java.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.803124Z"}
{"id":"988d3f62-c844-4278-9c8b-e6c9d169e434","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is 0, we don't perform the division; otherwise, the result is a divided by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805173Z"}
{"id":"b12f3fe6-b3fa-44f4-a90b-dc8eaeae8ebb","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The array of arguments is typically expected to be non-null when invoking main, as per Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.803381Z"}
{"id":"d13a1be6-67f3-44ff-b5cd-5bc815d6eed3","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE as a designated 'error' value.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805173Z"}
{"id":"13bb946e-5789-4785-83ef-7b5bf44d3eef","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + a % b == a","rationale":"For b != 0, the division and remainder relationship holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805216Z"}
{"id":"6b5ae4e0-c2e9-4f27-a9ef-d29d617ebd12","expr":"b == 0 || result * b == a - (a % b)","rationale":"If b is not 0, result equals a / b; thus, result * b is a - remainder.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805173Z"}
{"id":"c52a5924-58a2-4717-ba0f-a35d974d07bf","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length in Java is always non-negative, so this must hold for String[] args.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.803381Z"}
{"id":"6c0e65db-61c1-4d26-8f6f-0e5edc05d8a8","expr":"b != 0 || result < 0","rationale":"When b is 0, the result is Integer.MIN_VALUE, which is a negative number.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805173Z"}
{"id":"194f49af-d9b7-4881-9bf4-45c984a42688","expr":"b != Integer.MIN_VALUE || b != 0","rationale":"b can be Integer.MIN_VALUE or zero, but special care might be required in those extreme values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805216Z"}
{"id":"84d9dc60-9504-4776-ae45-cf6da5c98a8e","expr":"Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"The absolute value of the quotient (when b != 0) or the special value is always less than or equal to |a|.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-21T22:21:45.805173Z"}
